values ('e7f8a9b0-1c2d-4e75-8a45-5b6c7d8e9f25', 'information-design-visual-systems', 'Information Design / Visual Systems', 'Students learn to transform complex material into visual structures that make relationships, priorities, and actions easier to understand, and to study how people see, group, scan, compare, and misread visual information. The course builds layout, type, and color systems, then charts, maps, diagrams, scalable visual systems, interaction and dashboards, accessibility, research and information architecture, critique, and a polished multi-format information project.');

